S7-CONVERGENCE.md §4 step 1, Pi only (size 3 → 3, body now generic). The Pi member's
body (`main.rs:5273-5693`) is converted IN PLACE into `render_pass<W: RenderWait +
InputOwner + Furniture>(cpu) -> !`; `Wake`, the three traits, `ChannelWait` (the
channel discipline: `GUI_CHANNEL.recv()` + the GUI-CLICK-2 depth count + the [sched6]
bracket/census) and the `render_service` shim are appended at the FILE TAIL
(`main.rs:8627-8790`). Every edit inside the body replaces a line with a line
(13 hunks, all N→N; `git diff -U0 | grep '^@@'`), so no line below the body moves
and no panic `Location` shifts (PARITY §5.3). Everything added is gated
`cfg(all(target_arch = "aarch64", feature = "baremetal"))` — the Pi member's own
gate — so a tegra image cannot name `GUI_CHANNEL` and `pi`+`tegra` stays the
`compile_error!` at `arch/aarch64/serial.rs:23`; step 2 widens the gate.

The four substitutions of §3.2, as landed:
  1. `:5370` `let ev = GUI_CHANNEL.recv()` → `let wake = w.wait()`; `:5395` `match ev`
     → `match wake { Wake::Input(ev) if W::OWNS_INPUT => match ev { …the Pi arms… },
     Wake::Tick => strip_tick = true, Wake::Retire | Wake::Input(_) => {} }`. The
     Pi's `Event::Timer` arm is gone: `ChannelWait::wait` maps Timer → `Wake::Tick`.
  2. `:5497-5514` the serial-inbox drain is wrapped `if W::OWNS_INPUT { … }`
     (opened on the `SERIAL_WAKE_PENDING` line, closed by a folded `} }`).
  3. `:5525/:5528` `if W::STRIP && strip_dirty … else if W::STRIP && strip_tick`;
     `:5532` `pulsewin::service()` behind `if W::PULSEWIN` inside its existing cfg.
  4. `:5663` the [sched6] tail → `w.census(dirty)`; the accumulators (`s6_*`, `t0`)
     are `ChannelWait`'s fields; `:5366` `let mut w = W::new(cpu)` sits exactly where
     `s6_last_ms = arch::ms()` did, so the first span starts where it always started.

Choices where the design was under-specified (recorded in S7-STEP1.md):
  * `render_pass` is `#[inline(never)]` and constructs `W` itself (`W::new(cpu)`)
    rather than taking `&mut W`: the body keeps its own symbol and its accumulators
    stay register-promoted locals as before; a `&mut` to the shim's frame would be a
    memory object. The impl methods are `#[inline(always)]`.
  * The trait block is gated on the Pi member's cfg, not the §3.4 union: the body
    still names `baremetal`-only items (`GUI_RECV`, `SERIAL_WAKE_PENDING`,
    `shell_inbox`, `serfocus_witness`, `click1_dispatch`) directly; the union gate
    is step 2's, together with the cfg-erasure of those statements.

MEASURED (commands in S7-STEP1.md), knob-off Pi `./arroyo kernel8`:
  kernel8.img sha256 d73a8981… (TIP 2a04fb4a) → ade3e3ed… — the hash MOVES, for
  the cause stated before the build (design §4 outcome (b)): the monomorphised
  `render_pass::<ChannelWait>` sorts first in the root CGU (generic instances precede
  DefIndex-ordered items), which permutes the CGU's function order and shifts every
  relocation behind it. Section sizes are identical (.text 0xf4564, .rodata 0x35a64,
  .data 0x7e48; image 1,254,984 B both). Per-function comparison of all 1351 text
  symbols modulo relocation (`fncmp.py`): 1350 identical; the one that differs is
  the body itself (`render_service` 0xa08 B → `render_pass::<ChannelWait>` 0x9cc B,
  −60 B: the same 26 call targets, the same referenced-symbol set, one LLVM
  tail-duplicated drain block emitted once instead of twice, block order and
  register assignment re-chosen) plus the 8-byte shim; the −52 B net is absorbed by
  the 0x800 alignment pad before `__exception_vectors` (gap 1396 → 1448). .data
  differs in 0 bytes. x86 `UNAOS_WC=1` kernel: byte-identical (see S7-STEP1.md).
  GATE-FAMILY: `grep -c 'fn render_service\|fn x86_render_service\|fn
  orin_render_service'` = 3 before and after; `grep -c 'fn render_pass'` = 1.

